            "review_title": "Review at Jazz & Bar",
            "review_text": "None of Your Biz\nCanada764 contributions\n0\nMy 2nd and LAST time here. Put some seafood on your seafood pizza\nJul 2017 • Solo\nYou're in Da Nang. From your table you can see the fishing boats that bring fresh catch to the shore EVERY DAY. So you order a seafood pizza, thinking you can't go wrong.\n\nWrong. A small amount of sea life is spread over a cheese-laden pizza in tiny pieces. It's not that it tastes bad (it's actually not bad at all), but the few bits of seafood are so tiny you can't even figure out what kind of an animal they used to form a part of. This looks and almost tastes like a vegetarian pizza. And the price is not cheap !\n\nSERVICE personnel on the other hand is GREAT. Friendly & attentive.\n\nIt's not the kitchen's fault either, because the pizza tastes good. It is actually the kitchen\\s work that prevented this from becoming a 2/5 review\n\nSo, MANAGEMENT, just think what would happen if you put at least 1 whole prawn on there and maybe even a few visible octopus tendrils. People would LOVE it,word would spread, and the place would be PACKED.\n\nAnother thing. I am in Vietnam. You do have a wine list. It has about 40 wines from Chile, France, South Africa. But NONE from Vietnam. Granted, Viet wine is an acquired taste, but would it hurt so much to add 2 Dalat wines?\n\nYour Tourist-centered management decisions just LOST you a customer.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten July 27, 2017",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-04",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
